ְּׁרִים those who make straight their ways (|| דָרֶ֑ךְ עֹבְרֵי ) Prov 9:15 , א ׳בּוֺא go (tread) a path Isa 41:3 ; of course of locusts Joel 2:7 א יְעַבְּטוּן ׳לֹא they confuse not their paths (|| דְּרָכִים ); ׳א יַמִּים paths of the seas Psa 8:9 ; אֹרַח רוּץ run along a path , figurative of sun 19:6 . 2 figurative path, way , of course & fortunes of life Job 13, 27 = Job 33:11 ; 19:8 (|| נְתִיבוֺת ) Psa 139:3 (|| דֶּרֶךְ ) 142:4 (|| נְתִיבָה ) Prov 3:6 (|| דֶּרֶךְ ) 4:18 ; 15:19 (both || id. ) Isa 26:7 (|| מַעְגָּל ) so אֹרְחֹתֶיךָ דֶּרֶךְ 3:12 ; plain or even path ׳א מִישׁוֺר Psa 27:11 ; in two cases with a special reference (1) כַּנָּשִׁים אֹרַח Gen 18:11 (J) of menstruation; (2) אֶהֱלֹךְ אָשׁוּב לֹא אֹרַח a path ( which ) I shall not return, I am going Job 16:22 i.e. to Sh®°ôl , compare Assyrian name of lower world irƒit lâ târat , land without return , see Jr 10 ; Jr 65 . 3 figurative way , of mode of living, or of character Job 34:11 (|| מֹּעַל ) Psa 119:9 . Specifically: a. ways of ׳י , his mode of action Psa 25:10 ; b. of man's righteousness, called ways of ׳י Psa 25:4 (|| דְּרָכִים ) 44:19 ; 119:15 (|| מִּקּוּדִים ) Isa 2:3 = Micah 4:2 (|| דְּרָכִים ) compare ׳א מִשְׁמָּטֶיךָ Isa 26:8 ; also way of justice, uprightness , etc. ׳א מִשְׁמָּט Prov 2:8 (|| דֶּרֶח ) 17:23 ; Isa 40:14 (|| דֶּרֶח ), ׳א ישֶׁר Prov 2:13 (|| id. ), ׳א צְדָקָה 8:20 (|| נְתִיבוֺת ), 12:28 (|| נְתִיבָה דֶּרֶךְ ); so אֹרַה alone Isa 30:11 (|| דֶּרֶךְ ) Prov 15:10 ; note especially חַיִּים אֹרַח , path of life , in righteousness & enjoyment of God Psa 16:11 ; Prov 2:19 ; 5:5 ; 15:24 (opposed to שְׁאוֺל ), also ׳א לְחַיִּים 10:17 (on these compare Str 14:32 ); c. of wickedness , ׳א מָּרִיץ way, path of the violent Psa 17:4 , compare also Prov 22:25 ; ׳א רְשָׁעְים 4:14 (|| דֶּרֶךְ ), ׳א בֹּצֵעַ 1:19 ; followed by abstract ׳א שָׁ֑קֶר Psa 119:104 , so 119:128 (|| מִּקּוּדִים ), also with adjective ׳א רָע 119:101 compare Prov 2:15 ( עִקְּשִׁים crooked ) called ׳הָא עלָוֺם Job 22:15 ; note also ׳א אֵידָם 